From b6e21ea2073faa8e314493f8eff6d35aa125438b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:14:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] media: apple: add VXD (PowerVR MSVDX) probe and bring-up
 driver

R0-R2 rungs of the ladder in docs/periph/ds-video-decoder.md, written
from the iOS 16.7.10 AppleD5500 kext with the tools/ds-video annotation
tooling; every register offset below is reached by that kext through
CPVDECCore::ReadReg/WriteReg and was re-mined for this driver.

R0 (probe, read-only): power the ps_vdec genpd, map the single 1 MiB
region, request the level IRQ without arming it, and read core id/rev
(0x630/0x640), MTX memory config (0x500) and the MMU config registers
(0x1080/0x1084).  coreId high half > 6 gates unsupported cores exactly
like AppleD5500::GetCoreRev; entropy/pixel pipe counts come from
coreId[3:0]/[7:4].

R1 (apple_vxd.boot_firmware=1): boot the resident DEVA image on the MTX
exactly as the kext does - two "bring core into known state" variants,
the comms ring setup (0x2000..0x2030 bank), the MTX boot block
(0x6a00..0x6a18, in the kext order, with the double 0x6a04 stage
write), then poll 0x2014 for 0xa5a5a5a5 and read the build halves from
0x2024/0x2018.  The image is loaded from /lib/firmware/apple/
vxd-deva.bin and its sha256 checked against the REL_812.0_14_Deva
image extracted in the study round; the blob is Apple property and
stays out of the tree.

GART: 1024-entry directory, 4 KiB pages, entries ((phys >> 12) << 4) |
1 [recovered from AppleD5500::initialize_gart]; 512 page tables ("2GB
mapping" for this 2 GiB device) identity-map the low 32 bits of every
DMA address, with a dummy page behind everything unmapped.

The host<->MTX message ABI (ring indices confirmed at 0x201c/0x2020/
0x2028/0x2030 by the kext recovery path) is deliberately not used yet:
whether the firmware decodes or only schedules is the open question
that the R2 ring dump answers.  Submissions refuse with -EAGAIN until
then; a debugfs dump (mbox, regs) provides the observability.

Validated offline only: LLVM=1 arm64 build with a full kernel link at
this commit and at the tip, checkpatch --strict.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
